cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "srflux: surface-renewal sensible heat flux from high-rate scalar series"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bambach
    given-names: Nicolas
    email: nbambach@ucdavis.edu
    affiliation: "University of California, Davis"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5060-8781"
abstract: >-
  srflux estimates the surface-renewal sensible heat flux from a high-rate
  scalar time series using two ramp detectors: a Van Atta structure-function
  cubic (SR-VA) and a Haar wavelet front picker (SR-WL). Both produce an
  uncalibrated flux closed by a single dimensionless coefficient, so a fast
  thermometer or radiometer can stand in for a sonic anemometer.
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/nbambach/srflux"
url: "https://github.com/nbambach/srflux"
keywords:
  - surface renewal
  - eddy covariance
  - sensible heat flux
  - evapotranspiration
  - micrometeorology
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    A novel wavelet-based surface renewal analysis for sensible heat flux
    density estimations from radiometric surface temperature
  year: 2026
  journal: "Agricultural and Forest Meteorology"
